### flow policy

| | rule | what is wrong | fix |
|---|---|---|---|
| ✗ | [`pr.ticket.in_project`](https://github.com/17twenty/flow/blob/main/docs/rules.md#prticketin_project) | 2 linked issues are not on the board | add the issue to the project |
| ✗ | [`ticket.ready`](https://github.com/17twenty/flow/blob/main/docs/rules.md#ticketready) | 2 linked tickets do not meet the Definition of Ready | fill in what the ticket is missing, or move it back until it is ready |
| ✗ | [`pr.title.conventional`](https://github.com/17twenty/flow/blob/main/docs/rules.md#prtitleconventional) | header is not a Conventional Commit | write it as type(scope): description, for example feat(cli): add --json |
| ⚠ | [`ticket.not_blocked`](https://github.com/17twenty/flow/blob/main/docs/rules.md#ticketnot_blocked) | a linked ticket is marked blocked | clear the blocker, or say on the ticket that this pull request is what clears it |

**pr.ticket.in_project**

- #12 is not an item of the project <https://example.invalid/12>
- #13 is not an item of the project <https://example.invalid/13>

**ticket.ready**

- #12 is not ready: it has no "Acceptance criteria" heading — say how anybody will know this is done; it has no parent — link it to the epic or bigger piece of work it belongs to <https://example.invalid/12>
- #13 is not ready: it has no "Acceptance criteria" heading — say how anybody will know this is done; it has no parent — link it to the epic or bigger piece of work it belongs to; the tracker has it flagged as blocked — clear the blocker before starting <https://example.invalid/13>

**ticket.not_blocked**

- #13 is blocked <https://example.invalid/13>

Why am I seeing this? Each rule links to what it asks and every way to resolve it: <https://github.com/17twenty/flow/blob/main/docs/rules.md>

